    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0835" n="1793" xml:id="pg1793"/>

                <head>No. 18.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville
                            West to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 29,
                        1887</date>. (Received September 29.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that Her
                    Majesty’s Government have been officially informed that the British vessels,
                    mentioned in your note of the 3d of February last, have not been released, and
                    that I am instructed to inquire the reason for the delay in complying with the
                    orders sent to this effect, as stated in your above-mentioned note.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
